# Deployment policy

## Always ask before committing or deploying

This outranks finishing a task end to end.

- **Never `git commit` on your own.** When code is ready, stop and ask: "Should I commit these changes?" Commit only after the user says yes in that turn.
- **Never deploy on your own.** That covers `npm run deploy`, `deploy:backend`, `deploy:frontend`, the Render hook and wrangler. Ask: "Should I deploy now?" Deploy only after the user says yes in that turn.
- **Never `git push` on your own** either, because pushing `main` is the first step of a deploy.
- A yes to commit is not a yes to deploy. Ask separately for each.
- A yes applies only to the changes it was given for. Later changes need a new yes.
- A request to fix something or check data is not a request to commit or deploy.

## Default: one deploy, not many

When the user has said yes to deploying, release, or shipping changes:

1. **Batch work first** — finish the feature/fix across frontend and backend before deploying.
2. **Deploy once** from repo root:
   ```bash
   npm run deploy
   ```
   This triggers Render (backend) then Cloudflare Pages (frontend) in a single workflow.
3. **Do not** run separate `deploy:frontend` and `deploy:backend` in the same session unless the user explicitly wants only one side.

## Why

Render free tier limits are **monthly** (pipeline minutes, instance hours). Each backend deploy consumes pipeline minutes. Partial deploys waste quota and can leave production on mismatched frontend/backend commits.

## Before deploying

- Commit and push to `main` (backend builds from GitHub), but only after the user approves both.
- Never commit `.env`, dumps, or `backups/`.
- Frontend production API URL is locked via `frontend/.env.production`, `scripts/deploy.sh`, and `frontend/src/lib/apiBaseUrl.ts` — do not rebuild with localhost.

## Commands

| Command | Use when |
|---------|----------|
| `npm run deploy` | Normal release (preferred) |
| `npm run deploy:backend` | Backend-only hotfix (rare) |
| `npm run deploy:frontend` | Frontend-only UI change with no API changes (rare) |

## After deploying

- Verify backend: `https://tallypns-api.onrender.com/health`
- Verify frontend: `https://tallypns.pages.dev`
- If API routes 404, Render may still be on an old commit — check Render dashboard deploy log.

See `docs/DEPLOYMENT.md` for full workflow.
